<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Dong'ou</h1><p class="st-meta">192 BCE – 138 BCE · capital Dong'ou</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Yue kingdom in southern Zhejiang, ruled by a descendant of Goujian, whose people asked to be resettled in China after a Minyue attack in 138 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zou-yao">Zou Yao</a>, like the rulers of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/minyue">Minyue</a> a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goujian">King Goujian</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-yue">State of Yue</a>, helped the Han against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a>. In 192 BCE Emperor Hui of Han made him King of Donghai, known from its capital as Dong'ou, near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wenzhou">Wenzhou</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Dong'ou was a small coastal kingdom of Yue fishermen and farmers that relied on Han patronage. It took part in the Rebellion of the Seven States in 154 BCE but then killed the rebel king of Wu at Han urging. Little else is recorded of its government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/minyue">Minyue</a> besieged Dong'ou in 138 BCE, a Han fleet came to its aid. Fearing further attacks, Dong'ou asked to move into Han territory, and some 40,000 people were resettled between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> and the Huai, ending the kingdom.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dongou.jpg" alt="Dong'ou" width="320" height="337"><figcaption>Image: Perinbaba · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Minyue.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>192 BCE – 138 BCE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dong'ou</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zou Yao</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Yue local religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yue languages</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Donghai, Eastern Ou</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-165&amp;focus=dongou" aria-label="Dong'ou on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7404 983 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dong'ou lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7769 1191h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7724 1239h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7724 1239h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day China. <a href="/atlas?year=-165&amp;focus=dongou">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
